    "authoredBasis": "New written-mathematics choice diagram, not a recovered scan. Asset ID: choice-graph-pair-b.\nDeliberately replace the reciprocal curve y=6/x with y=6x in both panels; keep the original lines.\nMisread x^-1 as x, giving 6x=x-1 -> 5x=-1 and 6x=x+3 -> 5x=3. Coordinates follow y=6x. This is a reproducible wrong graphical construction, not a fabricated source fact.\nDeclared actual panel geometry: [{\"panel\":\"I\",\"curves\":[\"y=6x\",\"y=x-1\"],\"intersections_exact\":[\"(-1/5,-6/5)\"],\"intersections_numeric\":[[-0.2,-1.2]],\"intersection_x_labels\":[\"-0.200\"],\"line_window_endpoints\":[[-6,-7],[6,5]]},{\"panel\":\"II\",\"curves\":[\"y=6x\",\"y=x+3\"],\"intersections_exact\":[\"(3/5,18/5)\"],\"intersections_numeric\":[[0.6,3.6]],\"intersection_x_labels\":[\"0.600\"],\"line_window_endpoints\":[[-6,-3],[5,8]]}]\nEquation labels are uniformly omitted as a task-fidelity design: the stem supplies target equations, so learners must inspect graphs rather than match printed alternative formulas. This does not change source data or seek new human approval.\nSeparate reciprocal branches; x=0 is excluded mathematically. Algebraic window clipping is not a domain endpoint declaration. Segment approximation max error at 640 px: 0.037037037037037035 px.\nCurrent executable contract has no pointOnFunction/intersection/root-completeness assertion or analytic function object. Supported displacement/pointOnLine assertions must not be described as proving these unsupported constraints.",
